GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC12): the 3D at screen resolution, drawn by melonDS's OpenGL
renderer as one picture.

UC11's steady overworld drew the player on a layer of their own (patch 0022) so that the world
and the player were both exact at the software renderer's whole pixels; everything the DS works
out between them (depth, outlines, anti-aliasing, shadows) then came apart (the user's play test,
2026-11-14). With the OpenGL renderer's sub-pixel positions everything is one picture.

- GPU3D: HiresHook, called at VCount215 after the renderer started, on the emulating thread (the
  shim's OpenGL renderer draws the same polygons, the picture in between's too). HiresPosition in
  the wider picture's columns, signed and unwrapped (the guard band). With Hires, objects in the
  picture in between move by exact fractions and nothing is classified as attached.
- GPU3D_OpenGL: the wider picture's width, the hi-res positions at every scale, offset by
  GoldLinkBias to stay unsigned (the shaders take it back); GoldLinkRead reads the picture back.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

